-- 0014: vendor sell prices for custom 'Forever' items (ID >= 270000) that the
-- client prices by formula but the server rejected (item_sparse.SellPrice = 0).
--
-- Applies to the HOTFIXES database (mysql ... -D hotfixes).
--
-- For SellPrice=0 items without Flags2 OVERRIDE_GOLD_COST (0x4000), the client
-- shows the retail formula price: ItemPriceBase[ilvl] * ImportPriceQuality
-- * ImportPriceArmor/Weapon/Shield[slot] * PriceVariance * PriceRandomValue,
-- vendors pay 1/4 of it. Verified: 281322 shows 42c in the tooltip and computes
-- to 42 here (armor column is keyed by Material: 7=cloth,8=leather,5=mail,6=plate).
-- This patch stores that same tooltip price as the row's SellPrice, so the
-- server's CanSellItemToVendor check passes. 247 rows: every pricable
-- inventory type; items flagged OVERRIDE_GOLD_COST stay unsellable on purpose.
-- No backup table: INSERT IGNORE overlay rows only; undo deletes them.
-- Worldserver restart required (item_sparse loads at startup).


